// Dashed Barline Test
// The ONLY fixture that draws '!' (LilyPond's \bar "!"). Until this file the
// dashed barline was pinned by nothing at all — no fixture and no test used
// the character — so DrawBarline's BarlineType.Dashed arm could have been
// broken at any point and every snapshot would have stayed green.
//
// Written the ordinary way, with a space in front of it: that is the form
// LYS4009 leaves silent. Glued to a note (`c4!`) it is the same barline, but
// warned about — a LilyPond author means the forced accidental by that.
//
// The dashes straddle the staff lines (~2/3 dash, 1/3 gap per staff space),
// and unlike LilyPond the bar COUNT restarts here, so both halves are whole
// 4/4 measures rather than one measure with a subdivision mark.
title "Dashed Barline"
composer "Lily#"

tempo 120
time 4/4
key c major

part melody

phrase dashedBetweenMeasures {
  c4 d e f ! g4 a b c' |
}

phrase dashedThenOrdinary {
  d'4 c b a ! g4 f e d |
  c4 e g c' |
}

section Main {
  melody { dashedBetweenMeasures dashedThenOrdinary }
}

form main { Main }

score main "dashed-barline" {
  staff melody
}
